# Figma → web (pixel-perfect)

When implementing or changing UI under `web/`:

## Required inputs
- Need a Figma URL with `fileKey` + `node-id`. If missing — ask; do not invent screens.
- Default file if user refers to Project onboarding: `uvCRuWVVgWqmE55UVGV44f`.

## Mandatory workflow (before editing)
1. Load **figma-design-to-code** skill, then `create_session` for the file.
2. `get_design_context` + screenshot for the target node (and child nodes if response is sparse).
3. Read Figma **comments** on that frame (browser Comments panel if MCP has no comments API).
4. Reuse project tokens (`--ms-*` in `web/src/styles/calendar.css`) and existing components/assets. Map Figma values to tokens; do not hardcode random purples/spacings.

## Hard rules
- ❌ No layout/copy/icons/spacing “by eye” or from chat paste alone when Figma is available.
- ❌ No emoji/placeholder icons; use Figma exports / project SVGs only.
- ❌ On MCP rate limit / missing screenshot — **stop and report**; do not freestyle a “close enough” UI.
- ✅ Match typography, gaps, radii, colors, states, and CTAs to the screenshot.
- ✅ Treat `get_design_context` code as visual reference; adapt to React + existing patterns (no absolute-position dump unless required).

## Done criteria
- Visual pass against the Figma screenshot for the requested screen only.
- List any unresolved Figma comments and whether code satisfies them.
- `npm run build` in `web/` succeeds after UI changes.
